y science  work  um i mentioned those differences between  ground cherry and goldenberry  that it appeared that the golden berry  was more affected by both the  three-lined potato beetle  and the chlorina subflexa than the  ground cherry and actually the  three-lined potato beetle preferred the  fistulas  over potato it was the first time i grew  uh ground cherry and goldenberry in my  garden was the first time i had these  beautiful looking potato plants because  all the three-lined potato beetles went  to the ground cherry and goldenberry  but they definitely prefer the golden  berry  i um again i submitted a proposal to the  triad foundation to get some preliminary  information  um that we could we could use to go  after  a larger grant for this work we  started by doing an unbiased metabolic  metabolic profiling  of this material right now we've  completed it for leaves we're looking at  husks and fruit  as well we're using lcms and we're doing  three accessions each of  ground cherry and goldenberry this is  work again being done by  nathan rheem and we're collaborating  with frank schroeder's group and this  is bennett fox who is a postdoc in  frank's group  for the ground cherry we're using this  zl05 which is a line we got from the  netherlands um  g.o is goldie it's one that's available  through  johnny's select seeds and this is the  pineapple which is one of our accessions  from poland  and the golden berries is india south  africa and colombia  so just in brief um for the method we're  using a freeze-dried material  that we then extract and then we run  that on the lcms  these are two chromatograms showing the  differences between ground cherry and  goldenberry i mean that just what i want  you to take from this is very visual  and looking at the differences in the  number of peaks and the height of the  peaks  but please note that there are  differences in scale here so you can see  there's definitely a difference in these  metabolite profiles between t